hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19643","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub informed us from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Ubayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me from Uqbah ibn al-Harith, he said— and I heard it from Uqbah, but I retain the hadith of Ubayd more— he said: I married a woman, then a black woman came to us and said: I have suckled you both. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I married so-and-so daughter of so-and-so, then a black woman came to us and said: I have suckled you both, and she is lying. He turned away from me, so I came to him from before his face and said: She is lying. He said: Then how about it, when she has claimed she suckled you both, leave her from you."
"19644","Sufyan narrated to us from Ismail ibn Umayyah from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Uqbah ibn al-Harith, he said: I married the daughter of Abu Ihab, then a black woman came and mentioned she had suckled us. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and stood before him and spoke to him, and he turned away from me. Then I stood at his right and he turned away from me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, she is only a black woman. He said: And how so, when it has been said."
"19645","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Uqbah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Nuayman having drunk wine, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those in the house and they struck him with hands and palm stalks and sandals. He said: And I was among those who struck him."
"19646","Rawh narrated to us, Umar ibn Said ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me from Uqbah ibn al-Harith, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the afternoon prayer, and when he gave greeting he stood quickly and entered upon one of his wives, then went out and saw what was in the faces of the people of astonishment at his haste. He said: I remembered while in prayer some gold ore with us, and I disliked it should evening come or spend the night with us, so I ordered its distribution."
"19647","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Uqbah ibn al-Harith, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away when he prayed the afternoon prayer, then he mentioned its meaning."
